      "procedure": "Assay (nitrogen, Kjeldahl): weigh 100 mg sample in a Kjeldahl flask; add 5 g potassium sulfate / cupric sulfate / titanium dioxide (33:1:1), 7 mL sulfuric acid and, cautiously, 1 mL 30% hydrogen peroxide; digest until clear blue; cool, add 70 mL water and 30 mL sodium hydroxide solution (2 in 5) by steam distillation; collect the distillate (80-100 mL) in boric acid/indicator and titrate with 0.01 N sulfuric acid VS; blank corrected. Nitrogen % = (E.P x Eq.wt x F) / Wt x 100, Eq.wt = 140.1 µg N per mL 0.01 N acid.",
      "kind": "specific",
