    },
    {
      "question": "Identification test A (IR) specification reads 'The retention time of the major peak of the Sample solution corresponds to that of the Standard solution' (HPLC wording). Loaded as written; confirm the IR limit.",
      "source": "Crospovidone__STM- RM-0 Crospovidone.txt:44"
    },
    {
      "question": "Assay is a nitrogen content (%) on the dried basis, but the procedure has no drying step and the formula has no loss-on-drying correction. Confirm how the dried basis is obtained.",
      "source": "Crospovidone__STM- RM-0 Crospovidone.txt:49"
    },
    {
      "question": "Peroxides: the limit is an absorbance (NMT 0.35); the ppm H2O2 values are for Type A (NMT 400 ppm) and Type B (NMT 1000 ppm). Only the absorbance is loaded. The STM does not say which type the item is; confirm the type.",
      "source": "Crospovidone__STM- RM-0 Crospovidone.txt:46"
    },
    {
      "question": "Microbiological limits read 'Not more than 103 CFU/gm' and '102 CFU/gm' (superscript lost); read as 10^3 = 1000 and 10^2 = 100 CFU/g. Confirm. Micro methods only referenced to SOP C2I-91-128.",
